HONEST BOUNDARIES
  (a) ZERO payment capability and no network beyond loopback - a taken-back
      archive moves no money, and a buyer still cannot pay (no merchant id,
      server, domain, filing+ICP or miniprogram appid+secret).
  (b) zero product face, zero api face, zero gate number - what changed is
      what a failure leaves behind.
  (c) the rollback covers the measured state-write face only; an
      append_archive read-back failure is not rolled back (unmeasured, so
      not claimed).
  (d) the third stage value changes two existing arms' asserted stage
      (recorded above as JUDGED-CHANGED with the sentence unchanged).
  (e) a failed fold still writes a backup before the archive; it is removed
      only when the rollback lands. If removal fails the detail says so
      instead of claiming the backup is gone.
